  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_08. Let triangle ABC be a equilateral triangle where \u2220A = 60\u00b0, \u2220B = 60\u00b0, \u2220C = 60\u00b0. Let triangle DEF be a equilateral triangle with sides DE = 12, EF = 12, DF = 12, where \u2220D = 60\u00b0, \u2220E = 60\u00b0, \u2220F = 60\u00b0. Triangle ABC is similar to triangle DEF by SSS similarity with scale factor 1.5. Find the length of AB in ABC.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A designer is creating two decorative tiles for a mosaic. Both tiles are equilateral triangles. The first tile, ABC, has all angles measuring 60\u00b0 each. The second tile, DEF, is larger, with all sides measuring 12 cm and all angles also measuring 60\u00b0 each.\n\nThe designer knows that these two equilateral triangles are similar by the Side-Side-Side (SSS) Similarity Theorem, with a scale factor of 1.5 \u2014 meaning that each side of triangle DEF is 1.5 times the length of the corresponding side in triangle ABC.\n\nWhat is the length of side AB in the smaller tile ABC?"
}